format-version: 1.2
ontology: nodule
!
! Nodule cell-type extension to the Plant Ontology.
!
! The Plant Ontology represents the root nodule as an organ (PO:0003023) but
! has no terms for its cell types, so the two nodule-specific cell types in the
! Medicago reference marker file do not survive `CellTypeStandardizer`:
!
!     Nodule apex        -> dropped (no PO term)
!     Nodule parenchyma  -> generalised to `parenchyma`, losing "nodule"
!
! For a root-nodule symbiosis project those are exactly the cell types worth
! keeping, so this file adds them as first-class terms. It is merged into
! po_final.obo at load time (shared.utils.merged_obo_bytes), so the `is_a` /
! `part_of` lines below resolve against real PO terms and every ontology
! operation -- the standardizer's name lookup, annotate.py's parent/child
! collapse, the `too_general` descendant count -- reasons about these terms
! exactly as it does about native PO terms. Nothing special-cases them.
!
! Deliberately minimal: only the two cell types the marker files actually name.
! Adding speculative nodule terms nothing votes on would clutter the name
! lookup and risk mis-matching a future free-text label. Extend it from the
! data, not from the textbook -- one [Term] stanza per cell type a reference
! marker file introduces. `Root nodule` is NOT here: PO:0003023 already exists.
!
! Ids use a private `NODULE:` namespace so they can never collide with a real
! PO id. This file is version-controlled and reproducible, unlike po_final.obo
! (a hand-made import-stripped derivative that no script regenerates); keep it
! that way.

[Term]
id: NODULE:0000001
name: nodule apex
def: "The apical region of a root nodule. In the indeterminate nodules of Medicago truncatula this is a persistent meristem, so the term is placed under meristematic cell; its markers therefore roll up (weakly) to meristematic cell, which is the intended is_a semantics. Contained in the root nodule via part_of." []
synonym: "nodule meristem" EXACT []
synonym: "nodule apical meristem" EXACT []
is_a: PO:0004010 ! meristematic cell
relationship: part_of PO:0003023 ! root nodule

[Term]
id: NODULE:0000002
name: nodule parenchyma
def: "Parenchyma of the root nodule (the inner cortex / infection-zone parenchyma). Placed under parenchyma so it is recognised as parenchyma -- the child-wins collapse then keeps the specific 'nodule parenchyma' over a generic 'parenchyma' candidate rather than the reverse -- and part_of root nodule for containment." []
synonym: "nodule inner cortex" EXACT []
is_a: PO:0005421 ! parenchyma
relationship: part_of PO:0003023 ! root nodule
